<type>(<scope>): <subject — ≤72 chars total, imperative, lowercase>

# Body: one bullet per change. Aim for ≤6 bullets, ≤2 lines each.
#   - path/area: what changed, and why if it isn't obvious
#
# Summarize, don't transcribe. The diff is one `git show` away — the body
# exists to explain what a reader can't get from it.
#   - One module = one bullet. Merge sibling changes that serve the same
#     goal instead of listing them file by file.
#   - Say what the change accomplishes, not how the code does it. Skip
#     symbol names, snippets, literals, line counts and per-file diffs.
#   - Drop mechanical fallout: lint/format fixes, renames forced by a
#     change already listed, follow-up import churn.
#   - Single-file or otherwise self-evident commits may omit the body.
#
# Non-obvious motivation for the commit as a whole goes in a final
# "Why: ..." line (≤2 lines) — the trigger or constraint, not a recap of
# the bullets. Do NOT write "moved from X to Y" history — `git log`
# carries that.
#
# type:    feat | fix | refactor | perf | docs | test | chore | style | build
# scope:   backend | desktop | runner | installer | scripts | docs |
#          or a sub-module (companion | hub | main | gateway | tools ...);
#          combine cross-cutting with '+' (desktop+backend).
